; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Variable</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"146\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;n/a</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hypogonadism (virtually all)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Hypergonadism (exceptional)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 17; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 25.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"7\" width=\"945\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tumours without distinct cell lineage</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 18; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 127.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"170\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Plurihormonal tumours</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Multiple combinations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Multiple combinations</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"146\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Variable</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.8pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"146\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;n/a</span></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"color: black; mso-color-alt: windowtext;\">Variable</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 19; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"38\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 127.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"170\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Null cell tumour</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 99.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.0cm; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.75pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"146\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 109.8pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"146\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp;n/a</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 120.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"161\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">GH, growth hormone; n/a, not applicable; PRL, prolactin.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">a</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Mixed</span> tumours occur and represent any combination of tumours shown; the most common is mixed somatotroph&ndash;lactotroph tumour. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">b</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">GATA2</span>/3 refers to GATA2 and/or GATA3 expression. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">c</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Any</span> tumour type can be clinically non-functioning. <sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">d</span></sup><span style=\"mso-no-proof: yes;\">Hyperprolactinaemia</span> that is moderate can occur with any sellar mass that has suprasellar extension, interrupting hypothalamic tonic dopaminergic inhibition; however, this rarely exceeds 150&nbsp;ng/mL. Lactotroph tumours usually show a characteristic correlation between tumour size and prolactin levels, whereas other tumours that secrete prolactin do not.</p>",
